No — **RMSNorm size is not the difference**. Every RMSNorm is still width **H** (576). The dim change is only in **layer-0 Q/K/V**: they read **2H**.

### Regular Llama layer (target too)

Two RMSNorms, both **H**:

```text
h: [B, S, H]                         # residual stream

residual = h
h = input_layernorm(h)               # [B, S, H]   ← norm #1
h = Attention(h)                     # QKV: H → … ; o_proj → H
h = residual + h                     # [B, S, H]

residual = h
h = post_attention_layernorm(h)      # [B, S, H]   ← norm #2
h = MLP(h)                           # H → I → H
h = residual + h                     # [B, S, H]
```

Example (`How can I do`, S=4, H=576):

```text
h0: [How] [can] [I] [do]     each [576]
```

Attn/MLP always see width **576**.

---

### Eagle draft **layer 0**

**Three** RMSNorms — still all **H** (576). Different **inputs**, not different widths:

| Norm | On what | Dim | ≈ Llama? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `input_layernorm` | token embeds `e` | **H** | new (extra input) |
| `hidden_norm` | fused target HS `h` | **H** | ≈ Llama’s pre-attn norm on the residual |
| `post_attention_layernorm` | residual before MLP | **H** | same as Llama |

```text
e: [B, S, H]     # token embeds (shifted: emb of next token)
h: [B, S, H]     # fused target HS

residual = h                                    # residual stays on HS stream only

e' = input_layernorm(e)                         # [B, S, H]
h' = hidden_norm(h)                             # [B, S, H]
x  = cat(e', h')                                # [B, S, 2H]  ← only place width doubles

attn_out = Attention(x)                         # QKV: 2H → … ; o_proj → H
h = residual + attn_out                         # [B, S, H]

residual = h
h = post_attention_layernorm(h)                 # [B, S, H]
h = residual + MLP(h)                           # [B, S, H]
```

**Only dim change vs Llama:** layer-0 **Q/K/V input is 2H**.  
All three RMSNorms stay **H**. Norms are same width, different **inputs** (and separate weights).

